      "@id": "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/GP-001",
      "@type": "GovernancePrecedent",
      "title": "Bilateral VRC signatures accepted as partial GR-04 implementation",
      "decisionDate": "2026-03",
      "status": "proposed",
      "context": "DTG Credential Specification v0.3 introduced bilateral VRC signatures. RAHP assessed this as partially implementing GR-04 (Reciprocal VRC Requirement), raising per-edge Sybil cost without requiring full threshold signing.",
      "rationale": "Full threshold signing imposes a UX burden incompatible with EPIC-12 (UX & Human Workflows) at current tooling maturity. Bilateral signing accepted as an interim measure, with GR-04 retained as a future normative candidate rather than closed.",
      "linkedRisks": [
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/RK-ID01",
        "https://trustoverip.github.io/dtgwg-rahp-tf/id/RK-ID03",
